---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Resultados de las Primarias de Colorado 2026" description="Nominees from Colorado's June 30, 2026 statewide and congressional primaries, and what they mean for the November general election." ogCategory="democracy">
  <section class="hero-mini">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 data-en="2026 Colorado Primary Results" data-es="Resultados de las Primarias de Colorado 2026">2026 Colorado Primary Results</h1>
      <p data-en="Colorado held its statewide and congressional primaries on June 30, 2026. Below are the marquee races that shape Denver's representation in the state capitol and Congress, and the matchups now set for the November 3, 2026 general election." data-es="Colorado celebró sus primarias estatales y del Congreso el 30 de junio de 2026. A continuación están las contiendas más destacadas que definen la representación de Denver en el capitolio estatal y el Congreso, y los enfrentamientos ya fijados para las elecciones generales del 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
        Colorado held its statewide and congressional primaries on June 30, 2026. Below are the marquee races that shape Denver's representation in the state capitol and Congress, and the matchups now set for the November 3, 2026 general election.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-sublink" data-en="Looking for Denver's 2027 city races? See the Council Candidate Tracker and Mayoral Tracker." data-es="¿Buscas las contiendas municipales de Denver de 2027? Consulta el Rastreador de Candidatos del Concejo y el Rastreador de Alcalde.">
        Looking for Denver's 2027 city races? See the <a href="/tools/candidate-tracker">Council Candidate Tracker</a> and <a href="/tools/mayoral-tracker">Mayoral Tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Status banner -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="status-banner">
        <p data-en="As of July 1, 2026, the Democratic nominees below had been called by news organizations. The Republican gubernatorial race remained too close to call and could head to a recount. Results are unofficial until certified by the Colorado Secretary of State." data-es="Al 1 de julio de 2026, los nominados demócratas a continuación habían sido proyectados por organizaciones de noticias. La contienda republicana por la gobernación seguía demasiado reñida para proyectarse y podría ir a un recuento. Los resultados son extraoficiales hasta que sean certificados por la Secretaría de Estado de Colorado.">
          As of July 1, 2026, the Democratic nominees below had been called by news organizations. The Republican gubernatorial race remained too close to call and could head to a recount. Results are unofficial until certified by the Colorado Secretary of State.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Governor -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Governor" data-es="Gobernador">Governor</h2>
        <p data-en="Open seat — Gov. Jared Polis is term-limited. General election: November 3, 2026." data-es="Escaño abierto — el gobernador Jared Polis tiene límite de mandato. Elección general: 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
          Open seat — Gov. Jared Polis is term-limited. General election: November 3, 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Phil Weiser (D) — Nominee" data-es="Phil Weiser (D) — Nominado">Phil Weiser (D) — Nominee</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Colorado Attorney General" data-es="Fiscal General de Colorado">Colorado Attorney General</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--won" data-en="Won primary" data-es="Ganó la primaria">Won primary</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Attorney General Phil Weiser won the Democratic nomination for governor, defeating U.S. Sen. Michael Bennet. On election night Weiser led roughly 55%–45%." data-es="El fiscal general Phil Weiser ganó la nominación demócrata para gobernador, derrotando al senador federal Michael Bennet. La noche de las elecciones, Weiser lideraba aproximadamente 55%–45%.">Attorney General <strong>Phil Weiser</strong> won the Democratic nomination for governor, defeating U.S. Sen. <strong>Michael Bennet</strong>. On election night Weiser led roughly <strong>55%–45%</strong>.</li>
            <li data-en="Bennet keeps his U.S. Senate seat, which is not up until 2028." data-es="Bennet conserva su escaño en el Senado de EE. UU., que no se elige hasta 2028.">Bennet keeps his U.S. Senate seat, which is not up until 2028.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Republican nominee — too close to call" data-es="Nominado republicano — demasiado reñido para proyectar">Republican nominee — too close to call</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Kirkmeyer vs. Marx" data-es="Kirkmeyer vs. Marx">Kirkmeyer vs. Marx</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--pending" data-en="Uncalled" data-es="Sin proyectar">Uncalled</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="State Sen. Barb Kirkmeyer narrowly led political newcomer Victor Marx by under half a percentage point out of roughly 461,000 votes — a margin small enough that a recount was possible. State Rep. Scott Bottoms ran third with about 20%." data-es="La senadora estatal Barb Kirkmeyer lideraba por estrecho margen al recién llegado a la política Victor Marx por menos de medio punto porcentual de aproximadamente 461,000 votos — un margen lo suficientemente reducido como para permitir un recuento. El representante estatal Scott Bottoms quedó tercero con alrededor del 20%.">State Sen. <strong>Barb Kirkmeyer</strong> narrowly led political newcomer <strong>Victor Marx</strong> by under half a percentage point out of roughly 461,000 votes — small enough that a recount was possible. State Rep. Scott Bottoms ran third with about 20%.</li>
            <li data-en="The Republican winner will face Phil Weiser in November." data-es="El ganador republicano se enfrentará a Phil Weiser en noviembre.">The Republican winner will face Phil Weiser in November.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- U.S. House District 1 -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="U.S. House — District 1 (Denver)" data-es="Cámara de EE. UU. — Distrito 1 (Denver)">U.S. House — District 1 (Denver)</h2>
        <p data-en="Denver's congressional seat. General election: November 3, 2026." data-es="El escaño del Congreso de Denver. Elección general: 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
          Denver's congressional seat. General election: November 3, 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Melat Kiros (D) — Nominee" data-es="Melat Kiros (D) — Nominada">Melat Kiros (D) — Nominee</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="First-time candidate, democratic socialist" data-es="Candidata por primera vez, socialista democrática">First-time candidate, democratic socialist</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--won" data-en="Won primary" data-es="Ganó la primaria">Won primary</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Melat Kiros, a first-time candidate running as a democratic socialist, unseated 15-term U.S. Rep. Diana DeGette in the Democratic primary — one of the night's biggest upsets and a marker of progressive strength in Denver." data-es="Melat Kiros, candidata por primera vez que se postuló como socialista democrática, derrotó al representante federal Diana DeGette, de 15 mandatos, en la primaria demócrata — una de las mayores sorpresas de la noche y una señal de la fuerza progresista en Denver.">Melat Kiros, a first-time candidate running as a <strong>democratic socialist</strong>, unseated 15-term U.S. Rep. <strong>Diana DeGette</strong> in the Democratic primary — one of the night's biggest upsets and a marker of progressive strength in Denver.</li>
            <li data-en="District 1 is heavily Democratic, making Kiros the strong favorite in the November general election." data-es="El Distrito 1 es predominantemente demócrata, lo que convierte a Kiros en la favorita en las elecciones generales de noviembre.">District 1 is heavily Democratic, making Kiros the strong favorite in November.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- U.S. House District 8 -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="U.S. House — District 8 (Battleground)" data-es="Cámara de EE. UU. — Distrito 8 (Bastión en disputa)">U.S. House — District 8 (Battleground)</h2>
        <p data-en="Colorado's only true toss-up congressional seat, covering the northern Denver suburbs. General election: November 3, 2026." data-es="El único escaño del Congreso verdaderamente disputado de Colorado, que abarca los suburbios del norte de Denver. Elección general: 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
          Colorado's only true toss-up congressional seat, covering the northern Denver suburbs. General election: November 3, 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Manny Rutinel (D) — Nominee" data-es="Manny Rutinel (D) — Nominado">Manny Rutinel (D) — Nominee</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="State Representative" data-es="Representante Estatal">State Representative</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--won" data-en="Won primary" data-es="Ganó la primaria">Won primary</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="State Rep. Manny Rutinel won the Democratic nomination, defeating former state Rep. Shannon Bird in a race that focused heavily on immigration." data-es="El representante estatal Manny Rutinel ganó la nominación demócrata, derrotando a la exrepresentante estatal Shannon Bird en una contienda muy centrada en la inmigración.">State Rep. <strong>Manny Rutinel</strong> won the Democratic nomination, defeating former state Rep. <strong>Shannon Bird</strong> in a race that focused heavily on immigration.</li>
            <li data-en="Rutinel faces Republican incumbent Rep. Gabe Evans in November in one of the most competitive U.S. House races in the country." data-es="Rutinel se enfrenta al representante republicano en funciones Gabe Evans en noviembre, en una de las contiendas más competitivas para la Cámara de EE. UU. del país.">Rutinel faces Republican incumbent <strong>Rep. Gabe Evans</strong> in November in one of the most competitive U.S. House races in the country.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Attorney General -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Attorney General" data-es="Fiscal General">Attorney General</h2>
        <p data-en="Open seat — AG Phil Weiser ran for governor. General election: November 3, 2026." data-es="Escaño abierto — el fiscal general Phil Weiser se postuló para gobernador. Elección general: 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
          Open seat — AG Phil Weiser ran for governor. General election: November 3, 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Jena Griswold (D) vs. Michael Allen (R)" data-es="Jena Griswold (D) vs. Michael Allen (R)">Jena Griswold (D) vs. Michael Allen (R)</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="November matchup set" data-es="Enfrentamiento de noviembre definido">November matchup set</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--won" data-en="Nominees set" data-es="Nominados definidos">Nominees set</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Secretary of State Jena Griswold won the Democratic nomination for attorney general. Michael Allen won the Republican nomination. The two meet in November." data-es="La secretaria de Estado Jena Griswold ganó la nominación demócrata para fiscal general. Michael Allen ganó la nominación republicana. Los dos se enfrentan en noviembre.">Secretary of State <strong>Jena Griswold</strong> won the Democratic nomination for attorney general. <strong>Michael Allen</strong> won the Republican nomination. The two meet in November.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Secretary of State -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Secretary of State" data-es="Secretario de Estado">Secretary of State</h2>
        <p data-en="Open seat — SOS Jena Griswold ran for attorney general. General election: November 3, 2026." data-es="Escaño abierto — la secretaria de Estado Jena Griswold se postuló para fiscal general. Elección general: 3 de noviembre de 2026.">
          Open seat — SOS Jena Griswold ran for attorney general. General election: November 3, 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Amanda Gonzalez (D) vs. James Wiley (R)" data-es="Amanda Gonzalez (D) vs. James Wiley (R)">Amanda Gonzalez (D) vs. James Wiley (R)</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="November matchup set" data-es="Enfrentamiento de noviembre definido">November matchup set</span>
          </div>
          <span class="result-badge result-badge--won" data-en="Nominees set" data-es="Nominados definidos">Nominees set</span>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Amanda Gonzalez won the Democratic nomination for secretary of state, defeating veteran state Sen. Jessie Danielson — a legislator we track on our State Sponsor Tracker for her work on labor and worker-protection bills. James Wiley, unopposed in the Republican primary, is the GOP nominee." data-es="Amanda Gonzalez ganó la nominación demócrata para secretaria de Estado, derrotando a la veterana senadora estatal Jessie Danielson — una legisladora que seguimos en nuestro Rastreador de Patrocinadores Estatales por su trabajo en proyectos de ley laborales y de protección de trabajadores. James Wiley, sin oposición en la primaria republicana, es el nominado republicano.">Amanda Gonzalez won the Democratic nomination for secretary of state, defeating veteran state Sen. <strong>Jessie Danielson</strong> — a legislator we track on our <a href="/tools/sponsor-tracker">State Sponsor Tracker</a> for her work on labor and worker-protection bills. <strong>James Wiley</strong>, unopposed in the Republican primary, is the GOP nominee.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why it matters + sources -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="methodology-note">
        <h3 data-en="Why This Matters for Denver" data-es="Por Qué Importa para Denver">Why This Matters for Denver</h3>
        <p data-en="State executive offices and Denver's members of Congress shape the ground rules for the policies on our platform — housing finance, labor rights, immigration enforcement, and how elections are run. The primary also reshuffled the field: Sen. Jessie Danielson, one of the sponsors on our State Sponsor Tracker, ran for secretary of state and lost, and several of the night's winners ran explicitly on housing affordability and worker protections." data-es="Los cargos ejecutivos estatales y los miembros del Congreso de Denver definen las reglas para las políticas de nuestra plataforma — financiamiento de vivienda, derechos laborales, aplicación de leyes de inmigración y cómo se realizan las elecciones. La primaria también reorganizó el panorama: la senadora Jessie Danielson, una de las patrocinadoras en nuestro Rastreador de Patrocinadores Estatales, se postuló para secretaria de Estado y perdió, y varios de los ganadores de la noche se postularon explícitamente sobre asequibilidad de vivienda y protecciones para trabajadores.">
          State executive offices and Denver's members of Congress shape the ground rules for the policies on our platform — housing finance, labor rights, immigration enforcement, and how elections are run. The primary also reshuffled the field: Sen. Jessie Danielson, one of the sponsors on our <a href="/tools/sponsor-tracker">State Sponsor Tracker</a>, ran for secretary of state and lost, and several of the night's winners ran explicitly on housing affordability and worker protections.
        </p>
        <p data-en="This is a public-record summary of unofficial results, not an endorsement. Figures reflect reporting as of July 1, 2026 and will be finalized when the Colorado Secretary of State certifies the results. Corrections welcome — email us or open a GitHub issue." data-es="Este es un resumen de registro público de resultados extraoficiales, no un respaldo. Las cifras reflejan la información al 1 de julio de 2026 y se finalizarán cuando la Secretaría de Estado de Colorado certifique los resultados. Correcciones bienvenidas — envíanos un correo o abre un issue en GitHub.">
          This is a public-record summary of unofficial results, not an endorsement. Figures reflect reporting as of July 1, 2026 and will be finalized when the Colorado Secretary of State certifies the results. Corrections welcome — email us or open a GitHub issue.
        </p>
        <p class="sources-line" data-en="Sources: Colorado Public Radio, Rocky Mountain PBS, Colorado Newsline, NBC News, and the Colorado Secretary of State's official candidate list." data-es="Fuentes: Colorado Public Radio, Rocky Mountain PBS, Colorado Newsline, NBC News y la lista oficial de candidatos de la Secretaría de Estado de Colorado.">
          Sources:
          <a href="https://www.cpr.org/2026/06/30/colorado-primary-election-2026-results-live-updates/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colorado Public Radio</a>,
          <a href="https://www.rmpbs.org/news/elections/colorado-election-results-2026-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rocky Mountain PBS</a>,
          <a href="https://coloradonewsline.com/2026/06/30/melat-kiros-diana-degette-colorado-primary-results/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colorado Newsline</a>,
          <a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-primary-elections/colorado-governor-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NBC News</a>,
          and the <a href="https://www.coloradosos.gov/pubs/elections/vote/primaryCandidates.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colorado Secretary of State</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-mini {
    padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary) 0%, var(--color-secondary) 100%);
    color: white;
  }
  .hero-mini h1 { color: white; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .hero-mini p { font-size: 1.15rem; opacity: 0.9; max-width: 700px; }

  .hero-sublink {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .hero-sublink a {
    color: white;
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .status-banner {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
  }

  .status-banner p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .section-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .section-header p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0.5rem auto 0;
  }

  .candidate-card {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .candidate-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .candidate-info h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .candidate-tag {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .result-badge {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .result-badge--won {
    background: #dcfce7;
    color: #166534;
  }

  .result-badge--pending {
    background: #fef9c3;
    color: #854d0e;
  }

  .candidate-context {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1rem;
  }

  .candidate-context ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .candidate-context li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .candidate-context li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .candidate-context li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.85rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .candidate-context a,
  .methodology-note a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .methodology-note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .methodology-note h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .methodology-note p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .methodology-note p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .candidate-header {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
